<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Anchor: the CENTRE stays where it is; the body grows and shrinks both ways.

  A solid PIN bar down the middle of an outlined body, with an arrow leaving
  each end. The same vocabulary as the two one-sided glyphs — solid bar = held,
  outline = the body, arrow = the way it can move — so the set reads as one
  instrument in three states rather than as three unrelated pictures.

  This is the anchor that writes NO position: it is the default, and it is what
  the mode opens on.

  Drawn white and tinted at use; see EditorControlStyles.iconButton().
-->
